<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/glued.rs. std only. GluedLattice::hot(d, block n even, beta, lambda, seed): torus of side 2n; every plaquette crossing a block boundary appears as glued (ordinary, weight lambda) and blocked (closed by wrapping within its block, weight 1 - lambda), others are bulk (weight 1); general plaquettes = four links with orientation flags; incidence lists give staples (contribution C or C^dagger by the link's orientation); heat bath and over-relaxation over the wilson checkerboard classes with Philox streams (seed, sweep, link, 0); boundary_difference = sum over boundary plaquettes of a0(glued) - a0(blocked), so Delta_beta(n) = 2^d log Z(n) - log Z(2n) = -beta int_0^1 <boundary_difference>_lambda dlambda. Independent tests in tests/glued.rs: at lambda = 0 the blocks reproduce the exact 2D torus plaquette; the integral reproduces the exact 2D square defect. examples/defect_glue integrates by Simpson.
